WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:05.140
Every gas plan starts with your SAC rate: what you breathe in a minute, at the surface.

2
00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.850
You get it from a dive you have done.

3
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:09.650
Three things from that dive.

4
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:14.880
The gas you used: say a hundred and twenty bar, from a twelve-litre cylinder.

5
00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.870
How long: forty minutes.

6
00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:20.260
And the average depth your computer recorded: fourteen metres.

7
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:25.700
A hundred and twenty bar times twelve litres: fourteen hundred and forty litres.

8
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:28.510
Over forty minutes, thirty-six litres a minute.

9
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:34.300
At fourteen metres the pressure was two point four bar, so you breathed two point four times the gas.

10
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.410
Divide by two point four, and your SAC rate is fifteen litres a minute.

11
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.660
Do it for a few dives and use the average.

12
00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.940
Dive log works it out from each dive's profile and pressures.

13
00:00:45.190 --> 00:00:46.810
Free on the App Store.

14
00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:47.980
diver dot today.
